hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"13","[AI-translation] Aur Abu Umamah - radiyAllahu anhu - farmate hain ke Rasoolullah - sallallahu alayhi wa sallam - ne farmaya: Jo shaks har farz namaz ke baad Ayat-ul-Kursi parhe, usey jannat mein dakhil hone se siwaye maut ke koi cheez nahi rok sakti."
"14","[AI-translation] Abu Mas'ud - radiyAllahu anhu - farmate hain ke Nabi - sallallahu alayhi wa sallam - ne farmaya: Jo shaks raat mein Surah Al-Baqarah ki aakhri do aayatein parhe, wo uske liye kafi hain."
"15","[AI-translation] Talhah ne Murrah se, unhon ne Abdullah se riwayat ki, kaha: Jab Rasoolullah - sallallahu alayhi wa sallam - ki meraj hui to Aap ko Sidratul Muntaha tak pohanchaya gaya aur wo chhatwe aasman mein hai. Zameen se jo kuch oopar uthaya jata hai wahan tak pohanchta hai aur wahan se qabz kiya jata hai, aur oopar se jo kuch neeche utarta hai wahan tak pohanchta hai aur wahan se qabz kiya jata hai. Farmaya: {Idh yaghsha as-sidrata ma yaghsha} kaha: Sone ka parwana. Kaha: To Rasoolullah - sallallahu alayhi wa sallam - ko teen cheezein ataa ki gayi. Paanch namazein ataa ki gayi, aur Surah Al-Baqarah ke aakhri aayaat ataa kiye gaye, aur Aap ki ummat mein se un logon ke liye bakhshish ki gayi jinhone Allah ke sath kisi ko shareek nahi kiya, bade bade gunah."
